Z||000013||RAREW66||06-14-2001||11:12 PM||||My 26k mile 86 GT has all it's original black paint. There are a lot of Fiero's out there that have better new paint than what GM used in 86. The car is very shiny, but you can see that there is a lot of paint on the car.<P>My 88 Formula has weathered 249,000 miles with origianl Silver paint except the fascias, hood and right fender.<P>Fred||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fformula88||06-14-2001||11:19 PM||||My Formula has its original red paint on everything except the rear decklid and spoiler.... the original spoiler was ripped off, so the decklid had to be repaired and painted, and a new spoiler was painted.  My dads 85 SE has its original white too.  Both are in GREAT shape.... my Formula looks new after a good buffing!!<P>I think that the plastic body panels allow the paint to last longer than steel cars.  Even in hot sun, the car isn't extremely hot to the touch like a similar colored steel body.  This must have an effect.  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
